        raise NotImplementedError()

# Codon 0.19 lowers a class with subclasses to a plain pointer until an object
# of it (or of a subclass) is built, while its Optional is already the pair a
# class with subclasses needs: `Optional[BaseCondition]` None crashes its code
# generation ("LLVM: error: value doesn't match function result type 'ptr'",
# in opt_ref_new_rtti) in a program that builds no condition, and an action's
# `condition = None` is one (_expect_optional_condition, #263). Built here,
# once, whatever the scenario builds; the check never runs the program. Only
# after its subclasses: a class built before its first subclass is defined is
# lowered without them, the same crash the other way round, so the model
# builds no class a scenario may be the first to derive from.
BaseCondition("")
